  "story": "The icosahedral answer to the Octahedral Crown, and a jump from binary degree 12 to 60 -- the icosahedral rotation group has order 60, so 60 is the lowest degree any invariant ratio can have. Twelve spikes of order 5 at the icosahedron's vertices over thirty double pits at its edge midpoints. Full I_h symmetry (order 120), the largest here. Its features are order 5, so the derived transfer scale is capped: this is the piece the cap exists for, because a mesh cannot deliver the dynamic range an uncapped order-5 scale asks for. One pole is at infinity; eleven are listed.",
